<section class="am-extra-content section-padding"><div class="container"><header class="am-extra-lead wow fadeInUp"><span>The foundation of Islamic faith and practice</span><h2>Pillars of Islam</h2><p>Explore the five pillars of Islam and their place in faith and daily practice.</p><p>Foundation of a Muslim's Faith | The Five Pillars that Shape Islamic Life and Belief.</p></header>

<div class="row g-4 am-extra-grid">
<div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.00s"><span class="am-extra-index">01</span><h2>Introduction</h2><p>The Pillars of Islam are the foundation of a Muslim's faith and practice. They represent the essential acts of worship that every Muslim must believe in and follow to strengthen their relationship with Allah (SWT) and live a righteous life according to Islamic teachings.</p></article></div><div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.08s"><span class="am-extra-index">02</span><h2>1. SHAHADAH (FAITH)</h2><p>The declaration of faith is the belief that there is no god but Allah, and Muhammad ﷺ is His final messenger. It is the first and most important pillar of Islam.</p></article></div><div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.16s"><span class="am-extra-index">03</span><h2>2. SALAH (PRAYER)</h2><p>Salah is the performance of five daily prayers at specific times. It is a direct connection between a Muslim and Allah, strengthening discipline, spirituality, and obedience.</p></article></div><div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.24s"><span class="am-extra-index">04</span><h2>3. ZAKAT (CHARITY)</h2><p>Zakat is the obligatory act of giving a portion of wealth to those in need. It purifies wealth and helps support the poor and needy in society.</p></article></div><div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.00s"><span class="am-extra-index">05</span><h2>4. SAWM (FASTING)</h2><p>Sawm refers to fasting during the month of Ramadan. It teaches self-control, patience, gratitude, and empathy for those less fortunate.</p></article></div><div class="col-lg-6"><article class="am-extra-card wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.08s"><span class="am-extra-index">06</span><h2>5. HAJJ (PILGRIMAGE)</h2><p>Hajj is the pilgrimage to Makkah performed once in a lifetime by those who are physically and financially able. It is a powerful act of worship that unites المسلمين from around the world.</p></article></div>
</div>
